#step-review:round
{
  "$schema": "https://step-review.dev/schema/v1.json",
  "version": 1,
  "createdAt": "2026-10-12T09:00:00Z",
  "target": {
    "title": "Keep open links private",
    "url": "https://github.com/superegodev/superego/pull/166",
    "baseRef": "main",
    "headRef": "codex/private-open-links",
    "baseCommit": "4b40f2f62c0b9eab92ca59c6852861f4a283cd0a",
    "headCommit": "7893f7a590f23bfeccc975310bdf7e727d317e24"
  },
  "overview": {
    "summary": "Web links to Superego resources used to carry collection, document, version and app IDs in the URL path of `open.superego.dev`, so every click sent them to the server. This PR moves them into the URL fragment, which browsers never send: the CLI now generates `https://open.superego.dev/#deepLink=…` links, and the Open Worker serves a static page whose inline script reads the fragment and opens the `superego://` link.\n\nThe rest of the PR is CI: preview deployments for the Open Worker, production deploys on every push to `main`, and tighter permissions for the workflows.",
    "areas": [
      {
        "title": "CLI: link generation",
        "points": [
          "`get-deep-link` defaults to web links, now fragment-based.",
          "`desktop` still returns plain `superego://` links."
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Open Worker",
        "points": [
          "The server-side redirect is replaced by a client-side opener page.",
          "HTML responses get a strict Content Security Policy.",
          "Every path except `/`, `/privacy` and `/robots.txt` now returns 404."
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "CI",
        "points": [
          "PRs deploy an Open Worker preview, linked in the preview comment.",
          "Pushes to `main` deploy the website, demo and Open Worker; tags also build Electron.",
          "Jobs get read-only permissions and don't persist checkout credentials."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "readingPlan": "Steps 1 and 2 are the privacy fix and deserve the most attention. Steps 3 and 4 are deployment plumbing. Step 5 removes the Worker's tests and can be skimmed, but see its note."
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "cli-links",
      "title": "Fragment-based links in the CLI",
      "attention": "high",
      "intro": "`getDeepLink` now puts the whole `superego://` link, URL-encoded, in the fragment of an `open.superego.dev` URL, and makes web links the default. The help text and new tests follow.",
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "packages/apps/cli/src/commands/get-deep-link/get-deep-link.ts",
          "notes": [
            {
              "id": "n1",
              "kind": "explainer",
              "body": "Two changes in one: the link format (the deep link moves from the path to `#deepLink=`), and the default. Before, an omitted `linkFormat` meant `desktop`; now only an explicit `desktop` does, so omitting it gives a web link.",
              "anchor": {
                "side": "new",
                "line": 72,
                "text": "  return linkFormat === \"desktop\"",
                "endLine": 74
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "n2",
              "kind": "issue",
              "severity": "concern",
              "body": "The new default isn't reflected in the agent skill that the CLI installs: `packages/apps/cli/src/commands/agents/install-skill/SKILL.md` still says `get-deep-link` creates a `superego://...` desktop link. Agents following it will now get web links without expecting them. Update the skill in this PR.",
              "anchor": {
                "side": "new",
                "line": 72,
                "text": "  return linkFormat === \"desktop\""
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "n3",
              "kind": "issue",
              "severity": "nit",
              "body": "Missing blank line between the end of the command definition and the comment.",
              "anchor": {
                "side": "new",
                "line": 69,
                "text": "// Exported only for tests."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "path": "packages/apps/cli/src/commands/get-deep-link/additional-notes.md"
        },
        {
          "path": "packages/apps/cli/src/commands/get-deep-link/get-deep-link.test.ts",
          "notes": [
            {
              "id": "n4",
              "kind": "explainer",
              "body": "The expected URL shows the encoding end to end: the deep link's own query (`?view=App&appId=…`) is fully escaped, so it can't be confused with the fragment's `deepLink=` parameter.",
              "anchor": {
                "side": "new",
                "line": 18,
                "text": "      \"https://open.superego.dev/#deepLink=superego%3A%2F%2F%2Fcollections%2FCollection_abc%3Fview%3DApp%26appId%3DApp_abc\",",
                "endLine": 20
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "opener-page",
      "title": "Client-side opener page",
      "attention": "high",
      "intro": "The Worker no longer redirects. It serves the info page at `/` and `/privacy`, and that page's script reads `#deepLink=` and navigates to it if it's a `superego:` URL.",
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "packages/apps/open/src/worker.ts",
          "notes": [
            {
              "id": "n5",
              "kind": "explainer",
              "body": "The page needs its inline script and styles, so the policy allows exactly those and blocks everything else: no external resources, no forms, no framing.",
              "anchor": {
                "side": "new",
                "line": 11,
                "text": "  \"Content-Security-Policy\": [",
                "endLine": 18
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "n6",
              "kind": "issue",
              "severity": "nit",
              "body": "The script is static (`${deepLinkProtocol}` is a constant), so `script-src` could allow it by its `sha256-…` hash instead of `'unsafe-inline'`. Not exploitable today, since nothing user-controlled is rendered server-side, but a hash keeps it that way.",
              "anchor": {
                "side": "new",
                "line": 13,
                "text": "    \"script-src 'unsafe-inline'\","
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "n7",
              "kind": "issue",
              "severity": "concern",
              "body": "Links generated before this PR (`https://open.superego.dev/collections/…`) now get a plain-text 404. They live on in chat histories, and since [main now deploys production](step:ci) the break happens on merge.\n\nThose requests already contain the IDs, so a redirect for legacy paths would leak nothing new. Alternatively, serve the info page for unknown paths with a note that the link format changed.",
              "anchor": {
                "side": "new",
                "line": 43,
                "text": "  return textResponse(\"Not found\\n\", 404);"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "n8",
              "kind": "explainer",
              "body": "The protocol check is what keeps this from being an open redirect: `#deepLink=https://evil.example` or `javascript:` URLs are ignored. The link is shown with `textContent`, so it can't inject markup.",
              "anchor": {
                "side": "new",
                "line": 118,
                "text": "        if (deepLinkUrl.protocol === \"${deepLinkProtocol}:\") {",
                "endLine": 127
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "n9",
              "kind": "issue",
              "severity": "question",
              "body": "When `deepLink` is present but isn't a valid `superego:` URL, the page silently shows the generic text. Should it say the link is malformed, so users can report it?",
              "anchor": {
                "side": "new",
                "line": 114,
                "text": "        } catch {",
                "endLine": 116
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "open-previews",
      "title": "Open Worker previews",
      "attention": "normal",
      "intro": "Configuration for deploying PR previews of the Open Worker as Worker versions with preview URLs. The CI job that runs it is in [the next step](step:ci).",
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "packages/apps/open/wrangler.jsonc",
          "notes": [
            {
              "id": "n10",
              "kind": "explainer",
              "body": "Required for `--preview-alias`: without preview URLs, an uploaded version has no address of its own.",
              "anchor": {
                "side": "new",
                "line": 6,
                "text": "  \"preview_urls\": true,"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "path": "packages/apps/open/package.json",
          "notes": [
            {
              "id": "n11",
              "kind": "explainer",
              "body": "`wrangler versions upload` creates a new version without routing production traffic to it, which is what makes it safe for PRs. The removed `test` script and `vitest` dependency belong to [step 5](step:removed-tests).",
              "anchor": {
                "side": "new",
                "line": 8,
                "text": "    \"deploy:preview\": \"wrangler versions upload\","
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "path": "package.json"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ci",
      "title": "Workflows: deploys and hardening",
      "attention": "normal",
      "intro": "The tag workflow becomes `main-and-tags.yml` and also deploys on pushes to `main`. Both workflows get read-only permissions and non-persisted checkout credentials, and the PR comment is now posted with `actions/github-script`.",
      "files": [
        {
          "path": ".github/workflows/main-and-tags.yml",
          "notes": [
            {
              "id": "n12",
              "kind": "explainer",
              "body": "A release is usually pushed as a commit on `main` plus its tag, which triggers two runs. The `main` run skips itself when the commit already has a version tag, leaving the work to the tag run.",
              "anchor": {
                "side": "new",
                "line": 31,
                "text": "          git fetch --force origin \"refs/tags/v*:refs/tags/v*\"",
                "endLine": 38
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "n13",
              "kind": "issue",
              "severity": "question",
              "body": "The skip only works if the tag exists when the `main` run starts. If the tag is pushed later (e.g. after checking the deployed site), both runs deploy to production. Harmless if deploys are idempotent, but is that the intended release flow?",
              "anchor": {
                "side": "new",
                "line": 32,
                "text": "          if git tag --points-at \"$GITHUB_SHA\" --list \"v*\" | grep -q .; then"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "n14",
              "kind": "issue",
              "severity": "question",
              "body": "QA moves from `warp-macos-26-arm64-6x` to `macos-latest`, while the Electron builds keep the WarpBuild runners. Intentional? It will make release QA slower.",
              "anchor": {
                "side": "new",
                "line": 43,
                "text": "    runs-on: macos-latest"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "path": ".github/workflows/pull-requests.yml",
          "notes": [
            {
              "id": "n15",
              "kind": "explainer",
              "body": "PR comments go through the Issues API, so `issues: write` is the permission it needs.",
              "anchor": {
                "side": "new",
                "line": 189,
                "text": "      issues: write"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "n16",
              "kind": "explainer",
              "body": "Matching the old action's marker too means PRs opened before this change get their existing comment updated instead of a second one.",
              "anchor": {
                "side": "new",
                "line": 197,
                "text": "            const legacyMarker = \"<!-- add-pr-comment:add-pr-comment -->\";"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "n17",
              "kind": "issue",
              "severity": "nit",
              "body": "Only the first 100 comments are searched. On a long PR the marker can be on a later page, and a duplicate comment gets posted. `github.paginate(github.rest.issues.listComments, …)` avoids it.",
              "anchor": {
                "side": "new",
                "line": 209,
                "text": "            const { data: comments } = await github.rest.issues.listComments({",
                "endLine": 214
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "removed-tests",
      "title": "Removed Worker tests",
      "attention": "low",
      "intro": "Deletes the Worker's tests and its `vitest` dependency.",
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": "n18",
          "kind": "issue",
          "severity": "concern",
          "body": "The Worker got simpler, but it still has behavior worth pinning down: 405 for other methods, 404 for unknown paths, and the security headers. The opener script's protocol check ([explained here](note:n8)) is the security-critical part and has no test at all. Rather than deleting `worker.test.ts`, update it for the new responses and headers."
        }
      ],
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "packages/apps/open/src/worker.test.ts"
        },
        {
          "path": "yarn.lock",
          "summary": "Drops `vitest` from the dependencies of `@superego/open`."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
#step-review:diff
diff --git a/.github/workflows/tags.yml b/.github/workflows/main-and-tags.yml
similarity index 83%
rename from .github/workflows/tags.yml
rename to .github/workflows/main-and-tags.yml
index 7981bba..041fef0 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/tags.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/main-and-tags.yml
@@ -1,123 +1,168 @@
 name: QA and deploy
 
 on:
   push:
+    branches:
+      - main
     tags:
       - "v*"
 
 jobs:
+  detect-trigger:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    permissions:
+      contents: read
+    outputs:
+      is-tag: ${{ steps.detect.outputs.is-tag }}
+      run-jobs: ${{ steps.detect.outputs.run-jobs }}
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v6
+        with:
+          persist-credentials: false
+      - name: Detect push type
+        id: detect
+        run: |
+          if [[ "$GITHUB_REF" == refs/tags/v* ]]; then
+            echo "is-tag=true" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
+            echo "run-jobs=true" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
+            exit 0
+          fi
+
+          git fetch --force origin "refs/tags/v*:refs/tags/v*"
+          if git tag --points-at "$GITHUB_SHA" --list "v*" | grep -q .; then
+            echo "is-tag=false" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
+            echo "run-jobs=false" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
+          else
+            echo "is-tag=false" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
+            echo "run-jobs=true" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
+          fi
+
   qa:
-    runs-on: warp-macos-26-arm64-6x
+    needs: detect-trigger
+    if: needs.detect-trigger.outputs.run-jobs == 'true'
+    runs-on: macos-latest
+    permissions:
+      contents: read
     steps:
       - uses: actions/checkout@v6
+        with:
+          persist-credentials: false
       - uses: actions/setup-node@v6
         with:
           node-version: "24"
       - name: Enable corepack
         run: corepack enable
       - name: Install dependencies
         run: yarn install --immutable --check-cache --refresh-lockfile
       - name: Install Playwright
         run: yarn playwright install --with-deps
       - name: Check formatting
         run: yarn check-formatting
       - name: Check linting
         run: yarn check-linting
       - name: Check translations
         run: yarn check-translations
       - name: Check types
         run: yarn check-types
       - name: Test
         run: yarn test
       - name: Upload Playwright artifacts
         if: failure()
         uses: actions/upload-artifact@v6
         with:
           name: playwright-artifacts
           path: |
             packages/apps/website/playwright-report/
             packages/apps/website/test-results/
             packages/tests/browser-app-e2e-tests/playwright-report/
             packages/tests/browser-app-e2e-tests/test-results/
           retention-days: 7
           if-no-files-found: ignore
           compression-level: 0
 
   build-deploy-demo-website-and-open:
-    needs: qa
+    needs: [detect-trigger, qa]
+    if: needs.detect-trigger.outputs.run-jobs == 'true'
     runs-on: ubuntu-latest
     environment: production
+    permissions:
+      contents: read
     steps:
       - uses: actions/checkout@v6
+        with:
+          persist-credentials: false
       - uses: actions/setup-node@v6
         with:
           node-version: "24"
       - name: Enable corepack
         run: corepack enable
       - name: Install dependencies
         run: yarn install --immutable --check-cache --refresh-lockfile
       - name: Build website
         env:
           PUBLIC_DEMO_VIDEO_URL: ${{ vars.PUBLIC_DEMO_VIDEO_URL }}
           PUBLIC_DISCORD_INVITE_URL: ${{ vars.PUBLIC_DISCORD_INVITE_URL }}
         run: yarn build-website
       - name: Deploy website to https://sueprego.dev
         env:
           CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN }}
           CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID: ${{ secrets.CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID }}
         run: yarn deploy-website:production
       - name: Build demo-app for production environment
         run: yarn build-demo:production
       - name: Deploy demo-app to production environment
         env:
           CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN }}
           CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID: ${{ secrets.CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID }}
         run: yarn deploy-demo:production
       - name: Deploy open worker to production environment
         env:
           CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN }}
           CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID: ${{ secrets.CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID }}
         run: yarn deploy-open:production
 
   build-deploy-electron:
-    needs: qa
+    needs: [detect-trigger, qa]
+    if: needs.detect-trigger.outputs.is-tag == 'true'
     strategy:
       matrix:
         include:
           - os: warp-macos-26-arm64-6x
             arch: x64
           - os: warp-macos-26-arm64-6x
             arch: arm64
           - os: ubuntu-latest
             arch: x64
           - os: ubuntu-24.04-arm
             arch: arm64
     runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}
     defaults:
       run:
         shell: bash
     environment: production
     permissions:
       contents: write
     steps:
       - uses: actions/checkout@v6
+        with:
+          persist-credentials: false
       - uses: actions/setup-node@v6
         with:
           node-version: "24.14.0"
       - name: Enable corepack
         run: corepack enable
       - name: Install AppImage build dependencies
         if: startsWith(matrix.os, 'ubuntu')
         run: sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y squashfs-tools
       - name: Install dependencies
         run: yarn install --immutable --check-cache --refresh-lockfile
       - name: Setup macOS for signing and notarizing
         if: contains(matrix.os, 'macos')
         env:
           MACOS_CERTIFICATE_P12_BASE64: ${{ secrets.MACOS_CERTIFICATE_P12_BASE64 }}
           MACOS_CERTIFICATE_P12_PASSWORD: ${{ secrets.MACOS_CERTIFICATE_P12_PASSWORD }}
           MACOS_CERTIFICATE_P12_PATH: ${{ runner.temp }}/MacosCertificate.p12
           MACOS_TEMP_KEYCHAIN_PATH: ${{ runner.temp }}/MacosKeychain.keychain-db
           MACOS_TEMP_KEYCHAIN_PASSWORD: ${{ secrets.MACOS_TEMP_KEYCHAIN_PASSWORD }}
           APPLE_API_KEY_BASE64: ${{ secrets.APPLE_API_KEY_BASE64 }}
           APPLE_API_KEY: ${{ runner.temp }}/AppleApiKey.p8
